body_markdown:
React email localization works best when you choose the recipient’s language before rendering, keep translated copy outside the layout, and format amounts for that locale. With Unlayer Elements, one React layout can produce English and German order confirmations without maintaining two separate templates. Your application chooses the language and supplies order data; Elements renders the content; your email provider handles submission.


Start with a small EUR-only confirmation: a subject, three order lines, a total and a link to the customer’s order. We’ll render it in an existing Next.js application, preview both languages without sending, then add a controlled Resend handoff.


## What is the smallest useful localized email?


Use a TypeScript Next.js App Router application with React and React DOM 18 or later. Install the content package and sending SDK:


```text
npm     install   @unlayer/react-elements resend
```


Follow the


[Elements installation guide](https://docs.unlayer.com/elements/react/installation) for JSX configuration and keep your lockfile. This is code-first rendering, not the commercial drag-and-drop editor. There is no visual-builder SDK in this example.


Create


` emails/order-confirmation.tsx


` . The catalog holds complete English and German messages. Keeping both catalogs under one TypeScript shape catches missing message fields while you edit; it does not validate JSON loaded from a translation service.


```text
import     {
Email  ,     Row  ,     Column  ,     Heading  ,     Paragraph  ,     Button  ,   renderToHtmlParts  ,
}     from     '@unlayer/react-elements'  ;


type   Language     =     'en'     |     'de'  ;
type   Copy     =     {
heading  :   string  ;   intro  :   string  ;   order  :   string  ;
total  :   string  ;   cta  :   string  ;   footer  :   string  ;
}  ;
const     copy  :     Record  <  Language  ,     Copy  >     =     {
en  :     {
heading  :     'Thanks for your order'  ,
intro  :     'We’ve received your order. You can review the details in your account.'  ,
order  :     'Order'  ,     total  :     'Total'  ,     cta  :     'View order'  ,
footer  :     'Questions about your order? Reply to this email.'  ,
}  ,
de  :     {
heading  :     'Vielen Dank für Ihre Bestellung'  ,
intro  :     'Wir haben Ihre Bestellung erhalten. Die Details finden Sie in Ihrem Kundenkonto.'  ,
order  :     'Bestellung'  ,     total  :     'Gesamtbetrag'  ,     cta  :     'Bestellung ansehen'  ,
footer  :     'Fragen zu Ihrer Bestellung? Antworten Sie auf diese E-Mail.'  ,
}  ,
}  ;
export   type   Order     =     {
id  :   string  ;
items  :     {
name  :     Record  <  Language  ,   string  >  ;
quantity  :   number  ;
lineTotalCents  :   number  ;
}  [  ]  ;
}  ;
function     languageFor  (  requested  ?  :   string   |     null  )  :     Language     {
try     {
const   tag   =     Intl  .  getCanonicalLocales  (  requested   ||     'en'  )  [  0  ]  ;
return   tag  .  split  (  '-'  )  [  0  ]     ===     'de'     ?     'de'     :     'en'  ;
}     catch     {     return     'en'  ;     }
}


export     function     orderConfirmation  (
order  :     Order  ,     requested  :   string   |     null     |     undefined  ,     origin  :   string  ,
)     {
const   language   =     languageFor  (  requested  )  ;
const   c   =   copy  [  language  ]  ;
if     (  !  /  ^[A-Z0-9-]{1,32}$  /  .  test  (  order  .  id  )     ||     !  order  .  items  .  length  )     {
throw     new     Error  (  'Expected an order reference and at least one item'  )  ;
}
const   base   =     new     URL  (  origin  )  ;
if     (  base  .  protocol     !==     'https:'     ||   base  .  username     ||   base  .  password
||   base  .  pathname     !==     '/'     ||   base  .  search     ||   base  .  hash  )     {
throw     new     Error  (  'Expected a configured HTTPS origin'  )  ;
}
const   money   =     new     Intl  .  NumberFormat  (  language   ===     'de'     ?     'de-DE'     :     'en-IE'  ,     {
style  :     'currency'  ,     currency  :     'EUR'  ,
}  )  ;
let   total   =     0  ;
const   lines   =   order  .  items  .  map  (  item     =>     {
if     (  !  Number  .  isSafeInteger  (  item  .  quantity  )     ||   item  .  quantity     <     1
||     !  Number  .  isSafeInteger  (  item  .  lineTotalCents  )     ||   item  .  lineTotalCents     <     0
||     !  item  .  name  [  language  ]  ?.  trim  (  )  )     throw     new     Error  (  'Invalid order line'  )  ;
total   +=   item  .  lineTotalCents  ;
return     `  ${  item  .  name  [  language  ]  }   ×   ${  item  .  quantity  }  :   ${  money  .  format  (  item  .  lineTotalCents     /     100  )  }  `  ;
}  )  ;
if     (  !  Number  .  isSafeInteger  (  total  )  )     throw     new     Error  (  'Invalid order total'  )  ;
const   url   =     new     URL  (  `  /orders/  ${  order  .  id  }  `  ,   base  )  .  href  ;
const   totalLine   =     `  ${  c  .  total  }  :   ${  money  .  format  (  total   /     100  )  }  `  ;
const   tree   =     (
<  Email   backgroundColor  =  "#edf1f5"   contentWidth  =  "600px"   previewText  =  {  c  .  heading  }
fontFamily  =  {  {     label  :     'Arial'  ,     value  :     'Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif'     }  }  >
<  Row   backgroundColor  =  "#172536"   padding  =  "28px 32px"  >  <  Column  >
<  Paragraph   color  =  "#ffffff"   fontSize  =  "16px"  >  PAPERTRAIL  <  /  Paragraph  >
<  Heading   headingType  =  "h1"   color  =  "#ffffff"   fontSize  =  "28px"  >
{  c  .  heading  }
<  /  Heading  >
<  /  Column  >  <  /  Row  >
<  Row   backgroundColor  =  "#ffffff"   padding  =  "24px 32px"  >  <  Column  >
<  Paragraph  >  {  c  .  intro  }  <  /  Paragraph  >
<  Paragraph  >  {  c  .  order  }     {  order  .  id  }  <  /  Paragraph  >
{  lines  .  map  (  (  line  ,   i  )     =>     <  Paragraph   key  =  {  i  }  >  {  line  }  <  /  Paragraph  >  )  }
<  Heading   headingType  =  "h2"   fontSize  =  "22px"  >  {  totalLine  }  <  /  Heading  >
<  Button   href  =  {  url  }   backgroundColor  =  "#ff5a5f"   color  =  "#172536"  >  {  c  .  cta  }  <  /  Button  >
<  Paragraph   fontSize  =  "13px"  >  {  c  .  footer  }  <  /  Paragraph  >
<  /  Column  >  <  /  Row  >
<  /  Email  >
)  ;
const     {   head  ,   body   }     =     renderToHtmlParts  (  tree  )  ;
return     {
language  ,
subject  :     `  ${  c  .  order  }     ${  order  .  id  }  :   ${  c  .  heading  }  `  ,
html  :     `  <!DOCTYPE html><html lang="  ${  language  }  "><head>  ${  head  }  </head>  ${  body  }  </html>  `  ,
text  :     [  c  .  heading  ,   c  .  intro  ,     `  ${  c  .  order  }     ${  order  .  id  }  `  ,     ...  lines  ,
totalLine  ,     `  ${  c  .  cta  }  :   ${  url  }  `  ,   c  .  footer  ]  .  join  (  '\n\n'  )  ,
}  ;
}
```


The layout follows Elements’ wrapper → Row → Column structure. Its


[rendering API](https://docs.unlayer.com/elements/react/rendering-api) documents


` renderToHtmlParts


` and the returned


` head


` and


` body


` . The plain-text version above is authored explicitly from the same copy and values, including the order URL.


` lineTotalCents


` is already the complete amount for that line, not its unit price. This narrow example sums final EUR line amounts and assumes no separate shipping, tax or discount rows. Your commerce backend must supply the correct financial model before you extend it.


## How do you preview English and German without sending?


Create


` app/email-preview/route.ts


` . Next.js


[Route Handlers](https://nextjs.org/docs/app/api-reference/file-conventions/route) expose query parameters through


` NextRequest


` . This route uses one order and chooses only its presentation language.


```text
import     {   type   NextRequest     }     from     'next/server'  ;
import     {   orderConfirmation  ,   type   Order     }     from     '../../emails/order-confirmation'  ;


export     const   runtime   =     'nodejs'  ;
const     order  :     Order     =     {
id  :     'PT-1048'  ,
items  :     [
{     name  :     {     en  :     'Linen notebook'  ,     de  :     'Notizbuch mit Leineneinband'     }  ,
quantity  :     1  ,     lineTotalCents  :     1800     }  ,
{     name  :     {     en  :     'Desk organizer'  ,     de  :     'Schreibtisch-Organizer'     }  ,
quantity  :     2  ,     lineTotalCents  :     6400     }  ,
{     name  :     {     en  :     'Weekly planner'  ,     de  :     'Wochenplaner'     }  ,
quantity  :     1  ,     lineTotalCents  :     4500     }  ,
]  ,
}  ;
export     function     GET  (  request  :     NextRequest  )     {
const   message   =     orderConfirmation  (
order  ,   request  .  nextUrl  .  searchParams  .  get  (  'lang'  )  ,     'https://shop.example.com'  ,
)  ;
return     new     Response  (  message  .  html  ,     {     headers  :     {
'Content-Type'  :     'text/html; charset=utf-8'  ,     'Cache-Control'  :     'no-store'  ,
}     }  )  ;
}
```


Open


` /email-preview?lang=en


` and


` /email-preview?lang=de


` through your development server. Compare the heading, subject-building code, product names, button and amount formatting. Then try


` lang=fr


` : the supported-language policy intentionally falls back to English. An invalid tag also falls back rather than interrupting rendering.


